// How a HouseholdMember row came to exist (#276).
//
// Household membership is a bidirectional data grant — members read each
// other's game collections — so it is a trust boundary, not a placement
// within one. Every value below therefore names a path in which the JOINING
// USER performed an affirmative act. There is deliberately no value for
// "an admin added them", because no such path exists or is planned: that is
// the invariant this enum makes unforgettable, since a new call site cannot
// be written without choosing a value.
//
// `Open` join policy (#231), if it ships, adds a fourth value; it is not
// pre-added here because the policy is undecided.
enum HouseholdMembershipOrigin {
  // Household creation. The founder consents by creating (#210's create path).
  Founder
  // The household invited, the invitee accepted (#163).
  InviteAccepted
  // The user requested to join, the household approved (#231).
  JoinApproved

  @@map("household_membership_origins")
}
